{"id": "EUVD-2026-82307", "enisaUuid": "aed378e6-4ac8-3c8a-887c-1a4fabf8f2b9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni3c: master: Do not treat master device as a duplicate target\n\ni3c_master_search_i3c_dev_duplicate() searches the bus for another I3C\ndevice with the same PID as the reference device.  The search can match\nmaster->this, causing the controller itself to be returned as a\nduplicate.\n\nSince the controller is not a target device, it cannot be a duplicate of\none.  Exclude master->this from matching so that the function only\nreturns real duplicate target devices.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b25b755d59077dd9484ba1360b8fe6396e5ccfb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/533faf3d2e67ded0a62b7ba753c0fe993d1dfc26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d0cc00957292e353ad46039034cd8f82fc4f8057", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/150e71808d3715a0deefbb189c780d03fdbdc735", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dc1b3eeba7991905a5b5b8129ebea51be7d87b7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93199", "GHSA-c82m-2rvg-fqpm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1262e528-40be-31b1-90e2-b301afb35a67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <4dc1b3eeba7991905a5b5b8129ebea51be7d87b7"}, {"id": "4aafe20d-e9df-388d-b820-41becaf79a1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4cf59295-91aa-36f8-88d5-28561496fa24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <150e71808d3715a0deefbb189c780d03fdbdc735"}, {"id": "8cbb808e-ac05-37cc-9587-b716716d2a16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3a379bbcea0af6280e1ca0d1edfcf4e68cde6ee0 <d0cc00957292e353ad46039034